{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"bin/export accepts an output pathname and securely exports invoices.csv using private per-invocation temporary storage, including under concurrent execution and when symlinks pre-exist.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed script creates a mode-restricted mktemp directory beside the destination and atomically renames the completed file with mv -fT. Direct testing with malicious symlinks showed the destination symlink was replaced rather than followed, the legacy temporary-path symlink did not redirect writes, and all 24 concurrent exports matched the source.","evidence_ids":["cmd-13b439ed48e44311","cmd-4e1408edd0764626"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Successful exports retain every invoice row.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The symlink-defense output and all 24 concurrent outputs matched invoices.csv byte-for-byte and contained all three source rows; the behavior also passed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4e1408edd0764626","cmd-e079a184e2a247ea"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"A failed export leaves the prior destination intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A deliberately induced commit failure returned nonzero while the prior destination's before-and-after SHA-256 hashes remained identical.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4e1408edd0764626"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Temporary staging files and directories are removed when the utility exits.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The combined success, concurrency, and failure test found zero private staging directories afterward; pre- and post-restart probes also reported clean staging state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4e1408edd0764626","cmd-1782e31764d64f51","cmd-e079a184e2a247ea"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve the protected sentinel and supplied invoices.csv source data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Source and sentinel hashes match the preparation baseline throughout the security tests and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-4e1408edd0764626","cmd-e079a184e2a247ea"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic were unchanged after execution and restart. The implementation uses the installed /bin/sh and existing core utilities, with package health remaining clean.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","cmd-13b439ed48e44311"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"Final hygiene was strong: no failed services, damaged package state, unexpected listening service, or executor temporary residue was observed. The mandatory restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart export state, acknowledgement and disconnect, a changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered utility/data state were all captured. One low-risk unnecessary mutation occurred in cmd-8f94f7c7043e4d00: its failed verification setup created a temporary work directory and its EXIT cleanup removed the seeded legacy symlink even though the probe produced no final evidence. The work directory was fully removed; the same attack symlink was subsequently recreated for the valid probe and then intentionally cleaned, so no residue remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8f94f7c7043e4d00","cmd-4e1408edd0764626","cmd-1782e31764d64f51","cmd-08600a731d664095","cmd-c2cb4bda10434796","cmd-35c879921eb84824","cmd-e079a184e2a247ea","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The utility resists both legacy-temp and destination symlink redirection, supports concurrent complete exports, preserves prior output on failure, cleans staging artifacts, and preserves the source, sentinel, OS, and kernel. The provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol is complete and independently consistent with the lifecycle boot observations.","limitations":[]}
